Overlay patch 0008: iOS frame/tick cadence probe (M3 rev3).
Per rendered frame (present) records the wall interval AND the time spent
inside DrawAndRunGraphicsCommands (eng_ms). Per game tick counts sim rate.
Every 10 s logs SOH_PERF wall_ms p50/p95/p99/max, eng_ms p50/p95, rendered
fps, sim ticks/sec, and thermal state via spdlog (lands in Documents/logs,
pulled by scripts/pull-device-log.sh). __IOS__-only; desktop build
unaffected.
Honest naming: BOTH metrics include in-present blocking (drawable
back-pressure). wall≈eng means the frame interval is spent blocked inside
the render+present call (GPU-bound or pacing), NOT CPU-bound game logic;
wall>>eng means time goes to code outside the render call.
rev5 (VR R0): adds a rolling 1 s sim-tick rate beside the existing rolling 1 s
fps and exports both as SohIos_PacingStats — the engine-side two thirds of the
VR pacing triple (spec D10); the present rate is measured in the compositor
loop and joined there.

